🔹 Frequently Used Tuple Methods
1️⃣ count()

Returns how many times a value appears in the tuple.

nums = (1, 2, 3, 2, 2, 4)
print(nums.count(2))


Output

3


📌 Useful when you want frequency of an element.

2️⃣ index()

Returns the first index of a given value.

nums = (10, 20, 30, 20)
print(nums.index(20))


Output

1


⚠️ Raises ValueError if the element is not found.

nums.index(99)   # Error

🔹 That’s it 😄 (Yes, really)

Tuples have only these 2 methods:

Method	Purpose
count()	Count occurrences
index()	Find position

This is because tuples cannot be modified.

🔹 Useful Built-in Functions with Tuples (Very Important)

Even though these are not tuple methods, they are commonly used with tuples and often confused in interviews 👇

✔ len()
t = (1, 2, 3)
print(len(t))   # 3

✔ max() / min()
t = (4, 1, 9)
print(max(t))   # 9
print(min(t))   # 1

✔ sum()
t = (1, 2, 3)
print(sum(t))   # 6

✔ sorted() (returns a list)
t = (3, 1, 2)
print(sorted(t))


Output:

[1, 2, 3]
